Subject: [PATCH] Fix non-atomic append in the log file writer

Upstream PR branch: https://github.com/jwoglom/trio/tree/fix/atomic-log-file-append
Branched from nightscout/Trio dev @ cb9e0ff.

SimpleLogReporter's appender seeks to end-of-file and then writes. Those are two
separate operations, so anything appended in between is silently overwritten:
the write lands at the offset the seek returned, which is no longer the end of
the file. That is harmless while this reporter is the only writer of
logs/log.txt, and stops being harmless once a pump driver plugin - loaded
in-process, sharing the app container - mirrors its lines into the same file.

O_APPEND plus a single write(2) makes the offset-seek and the write one atomic
kernel operation. Two writers emitting 3000 lines each lost 1088 driver lines
and 15 of Trio's own before; 0 of 6000 after.

Apply from the Trio repository root:
    git apply TandemKit/docs/host-patches/trio-simplelogreporter-atomic-append.patch

diff --git a/Trio/Sources/Logger/IssueReporter/SimpleLogReporter.swift b/Trio/Sources/Logger/IssueReporter/SimpleLogReporter.swift
index 2a02082..24c1c69 100644
--- a/Trio/Sources/Logger/IssueReporter/SimpleLogReporter.swift
+++ b/Trio/Sources/Logger/IssueReporter/SimpleLogReporter.swift
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
+import Darwin
 import Foundation
 import SwiftDate
 
@@ -111,15 +112,38 @@ extension SimpleLogReporter {
 }
 
 private extension Data {
+    /// Appends to the log file with `O_APPEND` and a single `write(2)`.
+    ///
+    /// Seeking to end-of-file and then writing is not atomic: anything appended between the
+    /// seek and the write is silently overwritten, because the write lands at the now-stale
+    /// offset. That is harmless while this reporter is the only writer, but pump driver
+    /// plugins run in-process and share the app container, so a second writer on
+    /// `logs/log.txt` would lose its own lines and corrupt ours. `O_APPEND` makes the
+    /// offset-seek and the write a single atomic operation in the kernel, so concurrent
+    /// writers interleave whole lines instead of clobbering each other.
+    ///
+    /// The `.atomic` fallback is kept for the case where the file cannot be opened at all.
+    /// Note that it replaces the whole file, so it must not be reached while another writer
+    /// is active - opening with `O_CREAT` above means it only applies to genuine failures.
     func append(fileURL: URL) throws {
-        if let fileHandle = FileHandle(forWritingAtPath: fileURL.path) {
-            defer {
-                fileHandle.closeFile()
-            }
-            fileHandle.seekToEndOfFile()
-            fileHandle.write(self)
-        } else {
+        let descriptor = open(fileURL.path, O_WRONLY | O_APPEND | O_CREAT, 0o644)
+        guard descriptor >= 0 else {
             try write(to: fileURL, options: .atomic)
+            return
+        }
+        defer { close(descriptor) }
+
+        withUnsafeBytes { buffer in
+            guard let base = buffer.baseAddress else { return }
+            var written = 0
+            while written < buffer.count {
+                let result = Darwin.write(descriptor, base.advanced(by: written), buffer.count - written)
+                if result <= 0 {
+                    if errno == EINTR { continue }
+                    break
+                }
+                written += result
+            }
         }
     }
 }
